                <pb facs="0403" n="397" sameAs="frus:frus1939v04/pg397"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1163Am3/413: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-10-15T12:00:00+09:00">October 15,
                        1939—noon.</date><lb/>[Received October 16—6 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>522. Department’s 229, October 12, 5 p.m., to Peiping—Sisters of Providence. We
                    made formal representations to the Foreign Office on October 10. Circumstances
                    of this case were set forth as fully as possible; reference was made to effort
                    to impair American rights to carry on educational work; request was made for
                    immediate termination [of] interference and for investigation.</p>
                <p>Peiping please repeat to Chungking and Hankow.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
